.Dd September 13, 2026
.Dt RCGC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rcgc
.Nd remove leftover broken symlinks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm rcgc
.Op Fl afhnqVv
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This program removes the symlinks that
.Xr rcup 1
created and that no longer resolve.
.
See
.Xr rcup 1 ,
the
.Sx DIRECTORY LAYOUT
section, for details on the directory layout.
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
will print the list of broken symlinks, then prompt for a confirmation to remove
them all at once. This behavior can be adjusted with the
.Fl f
and
.Fl n
flags.
.Pp
For performance,
.Nm
does not scan your entire home directory by default.
It looks for broken symlinks first at the top level of
.Pa ~ ,
and then at any depth within each top-level subdirectory of
.Pa ~
that
.Xr rcup 1
could create across all tags and hosts. (The configured hostname and tags are
ignored because a broken link might be the result of changing tags or renaming a
host.) Thus, deleting or renaming the source of one of these top-level
directories, such as
.Pa tag-foo/bar/ ,
will leave behind broken symlinks that
.Nm
will not see by default. In this case, pass
.Fl a
to broaden the scan to all of
.Pa ~ .
.Pp
When a link is removed and it was the last entry in its directory, that
directory is also removed.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "-d DIR"
.It Fl a
scan all of
.Pa ~
rather than only the subdirectories that
.Xr rcup 1
could create.
.It Fl d Ar DIR
remove links pointing into
.Ar DIR
instead of those named by
.Va DOTFILES_DIRS .
This can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl f
do not prompt to delete links; assume a response of
.Qq y .
.It Fl h
show usage instructions.
.It Fl n
do not prompt to delete links; assume a response of
.Qq n .
.It Fl q
decrease verbosity. Implies
.Fl n.
Use with
.Fl f
to remove links quietly.
.It Fl v
increase verbosity. This can be repeated for extra verbosity.
.It Fl V
show the version number.
.El
.
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
Because
.Xr rcup 1
cannot create a link whose target path contains a newline, or a link with a
relative target path, these links are always left alone even if they are broken,
as they are assumed to have been created manually.
.Pp
Dotfiles that were copied rather than symlinked into their destination,
because of
.Va COPY_ALWAYS ,
must be deleted by hand when their source is removed. Neither
.Nm
nor
.Xr rcdn 1
will remove them.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev RCRC"
.It Ev RCRC
User configuration file. Defaults to
.Pa ~/.rcrc .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Pa ~/.rcrc
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl rcgc
.Dl rcgc -qf
.Dl rcgc -a
.Dl rcgc -d ~/corporate-dotfiles
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lsrc 1 ,
.Xr mkrc 1 ,
.Xr rcdn 1 ,
.Xr rcup 1 ,
.Xr rcrc 5 ,
.Xr rcm 7
